  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The table provides characteristics for two wires, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span>, which are made of the same uniform metallic conductor.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Wire</th><th>Length</th><th>Radius</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"L\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"r\"></span></td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2L\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2r\"></span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Wire <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span> and wire <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span> are connected in series to a direct current (DC) power supply that has negligible internal resistance. Which of the following is the ratio <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{V_X}{V_Y}\"></span>, where <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"V_X\"></span> is the potential difference across wire <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"V_Y\"></span> is the potential difference across wire <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span>?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.5\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4\"></span></p></li></ol>"
  },
